    "notes": [
      "Followed: the interior photo is now the main image, spanning all 12 columns and 5 rows (rows 5–9), the largest element on the page. It could go one row larger. Extend it into row 4 or row 10 if the headline or bottom band can give up a row.",
      "Headline spans 12 of 12 columns across rows 2–4, but the letterforms only fill about the top two rows. Row 4 is mostly empty air above the photo. Either set the name larger so the descender of the ç reaches the row 4 baseline, or end the headline at row 3 and start the photo in row 4.",
      "The headline is thin-weight at large size against a dense, dark full-width photo. The photo pulls the eye first. That is acceptable for this idea, but it makes the name feel secondary. A slightly heavier weight would keep the name first in the reading order.",
      "Nearby-list sits in rows 11–12, but its first line starts roughly a full row below the label in row 10. That leaves a dead module gap. Move the list up to start on the first baseline of row 11 directly under the label, or hang the label at the top of row 11 alongside it.",
      "Body spans columns 4–7 and runs about 45 characters per line, with a good rag. Its top baseline should align with the nearby-label in columns 8–12; it currently sits slightly lower. Snap both to the first baseline of row 10.",
      "Pinfield occupies columns 1–3 in rows 10–12, and some dots drift left of the column 1 edge into the margin. Clip or rescale the field so all pins sit inside columns 1–3.",
      "Columns 4–7 in row 12 are empty under the body. That is a meaningful empty module, so keep it. Do not fill it.",
      "The red accent is used only on the label, the list numerals and the current pin. That is disciplined. The photo's deep blue and the warm paper sit well together, so no change is needed."
    ],
    "summary": "A clean, well-proportioned layout that delivers Dan's request: the interior photo runs full width and large. Two things need tightening: the slack row under the headline and the gap between the nearby-label and the list in columns 8–12. Pull the photo or the headline up to use row 4, and snap the bottom-band texts to shared baselines.",
    "mean": 7.3
